    "body": "> Can you please provide a bit more detail, perhaps a demonstration or reproduction of the issue?\r\n\r\nSure! There you go: https://codesandbox.io/s/dialog-cut-off-qlg3y5\r\n\r\nIf you hover the info icon, a tooltip is shown, but it is cut off and the dialog gets a horizontal scrollbar.\r\n\r\nIf you open the combobox, the dropdown will be cut off and the dialog gets a horizontal scrollbar.\r\n\r\nThe desired behaviour would be, that those elements (tooltip / dropdown) would overflow the boundaries of the dialog. But setting `overflow: visible` is also not the desired way to go, because for other elements you might wish to have a scrollbar inside the dialog. For example if the dialog has a lot of contents (and the combobox is at the bottom).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1773229192/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
