    "updated_at": "2023-10-20T19:07:11Z",
    "body": "@tabatkins @keithamus Yeah i have been afraid this is the answer. It's just not realistic to convert all those components to popovers. We are using 3rd party libraries for a lot of those components, which we cannot influence that much (or it would just be too much work).\r\n\r\nWhat about a prop/attribute, that allows to put elements into the top-level space easily? Something like..\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div class=\"tooltip\" top-level>Haha</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor now we have applied a different solution. We simply moved the scrollbar to the backdrop by having an inner div. So the dialog element itself will stretch over the full screen and the inner div will be displayed as the actual dialog window. This works, but we don't like it, because we would prefer to use native-only features.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
