    "updated_at": "2023-10-20T19:23:34Z",
    "body": "> What about a prop/attribute, that allows to put elements into the top-level space easily? Something like..\r\n> \r\n> ```html\r\n> <div class=\"tooltip\" top-level>Haha</div>\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThis looks a lot like the popover API:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div class=\"tooltip\" popover>Haha</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\n> For now we have applied a different solution. This works, but we don't like it, because we would prefer to use native-only features.\r\n\r\nThat's awesome that you found a different solution! Hopefully MUI can adopt native `popover`, which I would recommend as the native solution.",
